## How to Structure the Evening

One of the most common mistakes with bachelorette parties is over-scheduling. Two or three strong activities beat five rushed ones every time. A structure that tends to work well:

**Start with something active** to get the group moving and talking. The VR arena or physical challenge rooms are good openers — they're immediately engaging and don't require much warm-up.

**Build in a natural break** with food and drinks. Infusion Play has handmade bubble tea, ice cream, and Bingsu on-site, so you don't need to leave the venue to refuel.

**Finish with something lighter** — the arcade lounge, where the group can wind down, compare scores, and cash in any points earned during the session.

If you're planning to continue the night elsewhere, the Yates St location puts you within easy walking distance of the rest of Downtown Victoria's nightlife.

